.TITLE "tar"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Creates and manipulates file archives. It is primarily used to __compress__ files for storage or __bundle__ multiple items together for easy distribution.

.DIV "TLDR"
**tar -c -f archive.tar files**
Creates a new uncompressed archive from the specified files.
> __-c__ create flag | __-f__ file flag | __archive.tar__ target name

**tar -x -f archive.tar**
Extracts the contents of an archive into the current directory.
> __-x__ extract flag | __-f__ file flag | __archive.tar__ source archive

**tar -c -z -f archive.tar.gz files**
Creates a compressed archive using the gzip algorithm.
> __-c__ create | __-z__ gzip flag | __-f__ file | __archive.tar.gz__ target

**tar -x -z -f archive.tar.gz**
Extracts a gzip-compressed archive.
> __-x__ extract | __-z__ gzip flag | __-f__ file | __archive.tar.gz__ source

**tar -t -f archive.tar**
Lists the contents of an archive without extracting them.
> __-t__ list flag | __-f__ file flag | __archive.tar__ source archive

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Always decouple your flags (e.g., use __-x -v -f__ instead of __-xvf__) to ensure compatibility with all parsers. Compressing archives with __-z__ (gzip) or __-j__ (bzip2) is a great way to save disk space when sharing large sets of files.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"


documentation: __https://www.gnu.org/software/tar__
